 confianza del 95 % de 5,6 a 7,2. El contrato [1], de 14.904 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: la acumulación de importes junto al límite es un indicador estadístico. No prueba que se haya partido ningún contrato ni que alguien haya actuado mal; puede deberse a precios de mercado, a presupuestos cerrados o a necesidades distintas.\nQué se puede revisar: en los expedientes enlazados, qué se contrató en cada caso y en qué fechas, y si varios contratos atienden una misma necesidad que pudo contratarse de una vez.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 552 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 87.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 6.3, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.6 to 7.2. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 11% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 347 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,904 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar distribution occurs in other months. The number of different contractors does not prove irregularities, as multiple vendors can be needed for different services.\nWhat can be checked: Check if December contracts are part of a larger pattern. Verify if awardee A has other contracts for similar services. Review contract [1] to see if the amount is standard for the service provided.","origen_es":"plantilla","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["w8MVPOdlhmHL1rX3q%2FMAPA%3D%3D","PnOsjcHkg5pSYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D","V0sQDkGvo24Xhk1FZxEyvw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}